== Storyline notes ==

* '''The truth-teller bumped.''' Takagi's forearm in the opening minute ended Jusuf's aura of unbumpability. The match did not expose Jusuf — he locked in the mosaraza kneebar twice and had the Dragon in real trouble both times — but it answered the tournament's first question: Jusuf can be made to fall. His Round 3 opponent is [[KAZUKI (wrestler)|KAZUKI]] in Aizawa — the block favourite against the man whose questions have just begun.
* '''Ishida's answer.''' The standing ovation at Ishida's entrance and the ovation after his win were the emotional peaks of the night. Eight days after the fastest loss of the tournament, the veteran submitted the Hammer with the hold that made him a champion. The plan works — it just needed the right opponent.
* '''The three-way lead.''' KAZUKI, Takagi, and Taumafa all sit at 4 points, undefeated. Round 3 in Aizawa splits the trio: KAZUKI faces Jusuf, Taumafa faces Diallo, and Takagi faces Tanaka. Only KAZUKI's match is against a fellow contender.
* '''The 0-2 tier is a lie.''' Kuroki (two strong performances), Reyes (two competitive losses), and Ono (flash cradle at 2.8, the crowd behind him) all sit at zero points — but none of the three has looked overmatched. The block's bottom half is better than its record.
* '''Taumafa's quiet perfection.''' Two wins, no points dropped, no headlines. The Strong Openweight Champion is 2-0 and enters Round 3 against Diallo — the family warrior against the Cannon Club's Hammer, with family pride on the line.

